@startuml architecture
' Render from the repository root:
' plantuml -tsvg -nometadata docs/assets/architecture.puml

title collab-ai · Shared broker and dev workspace

<style>
title {
    FontSize 25
}
document {
    Margin 24
    BackgroundColor #fafafa
}
rectangle {
    LineStyle 5
    LineColor #grey
    LineThickness 2
}
.HumanControl {
    BackgroundColor #fff3b0
}
.Control {
    BackgroundColor #e3efff
}
.Dev {
    BackgroundColor #e7f5eb
}
.Socket {
    BackgroundColor #fce4f0
}
.Storage {
    BackgroundColor #f0eaff
}
legend {
    FontSize 15
    Padding 12
}
</style>

hide stereotype
skinparam {
    backgroundColor #fafafa
    shadowing false
    componentStyle rectangle
    defaultFontSize 16
    padding 10
    nodesep 40
    ranksep 35
}

actor "You · host terminals" as Human

rectangle "workspace · dev container\nNetwork access by default · opt-out available" as Dev {
    component "=Codex\nTerminal + collab-codex\nManaged proxy / listener" as Codex <<Dev>>
    component "=Claude Code\nTerminal + collab-mcp\nMCP over stdin / stdout" as Claude <<Dev>>
    component "=Persistent workspace\n/workspace · independent Incus volume\nOptional: selected host directory\nMac host mounts: read-only\n--\nSandbox data owned by agent (1001:1001)\nLinux writes: dedicated host-sharing account\nRun shell commands, builds and tests inside dev" as Project <<Dev>>
    file "=Persistent agent home\n/home/agent on a separate Incus volume\nSurvives container replacement\nCodex + Claude settings, skills, memory and sessions\n--\nAgents update sandbox-owned state\nSelected host-state import tooling · future\nNo live host-home sync" as AgentHome <<Storage>>
    file "=broker.sock · Unix socket\n/mnt/collab-ipc/broker.sock\nDirectory mounted READ-ONLY in dev\nOwner: broker · group: collab-clients\nSocket mode: 0660\n--\nClients may connect and send requests\nCannot replace or remove the socket" as Socket <<Socket>>
}

rectangle "secured · control container\nOffline · no network interface" as Control {
    component "=Human controls\ncollab dashboard · collab status\nOperator settings stay here" as Dashboard <<HumanControl>>
    component "=One collab-ai broker\nCreates / listens on broker.sock\nOnly process accessing SQLite" as Broker <<Control>>
    database "=One collaboration SQLite database\nPrivate persistent volume\nNever mounted in dev" as DB <<Control>>
}

Human -down-> Codex : SSH · prompts / output
Human -down-> Claude : SSH · prompts / output
Human -down-> Dashboard : Host-administered terminal

Codex -down-> Socket : Broker protocol
Claude -down-> Socket : Broker protocol
Socket -[hidden]down-> Project
Project -[hidden]down-> AgentHome

Dashboard -down-> Broker : Queries via the same local UDS
Broker <-left-> Socket : Same shared Incus volume\n/mnt/collab-ipc\nREAD-WRITE mount in control
Broker -down-> DB : Read / write

legend bottom
    <back:#e7f5eb> Agents in dev </back>   <back:#e3efff> Services in control </back>   <back:#fce4f0> One shared Unix socket </back>   <back:#fff3b0> Human controls </back>
    Directory: broker:collab-clients, 0750. Socket: broker:collab-clients, 0660.
    Broker UID 1002 / client GID 1003 are mapped by the shifted IPC volume; directory mounted at boot.
    Read-only mount protects the socket path. It does not prevent sending socket requests.
    Dev clients share access; this does not isolate Codex from Claude or other code running as their user.
    Workspace and agent-home volumes survive replacement; Terraform blocks their deletion until explicitly allowed.
    Host mounts do not prevent execution. Writable sharing allows changes to host scripts and configuration.
    Host-state import remains future work. File retention is not a resume guarantee.
endlegend

@enduml
